    "number": 452,
    "title": "Share bounded session titles and project names across Hub metadata",
    "body": "## Problem and resulting change\n\nRefs #424. Shared sessions currently expose a label or ID even when the provider has a title. Lifecycle 1.1 adds bounded title/source and project display metadata; the owner persists it and Hub HTTP/MCP and B.U.N.N.Y. expose snapshot 1.2. Explicit user labels retain precedence. Default snapshot 1.0 and opt-in 1.1 retain their closed shapes.\n\n## Scope and dependencies\n\nThe owner approved the field design before producer changes ([decision](https://github.com/jimmie-potts/agent-device-hub/issues/424#issuecomment-5843666785)). Titles allow 160 Unicode scalars; labels/projects allow 80. Hook configurations explicitly opt into lifecycle 1.1; existing configurations stay 1.0. Policy permits the scoped content while excluding credentials; #425 prompt/response/transcript-content capture is not implemented.\n\nSource-only: no installed hooks, settings changes, live migration, agent sessions or device operations. Hub #426, Pixoo #106 and Nanoleaf #179 adopt the released prerequisite separately. Package candidates are lifecycle 1.1.0, agent-state 3.3.0 and Hub 0.4.0. Historical vendor archives and source pins are unchanged. Publication follows guarded merge and verified main CI, with immutable checksums and source receipts.\n\nState/recovery walkthrough: the existing owner and exclusive storage lease remain authoritative. The new reader limits files to 1 MiB, 8,192 lines, 64 KiB per record and 100 ms inside the existing process deadline, with at most four unsettled reads. Missing metadata preserves lifecycle delivery. Rename fixtures show that metadata-only updates do not refresh lifecycle evidence; explicit user labels survive agent labels and legacy import. Durable 2.1 imports 1.0/2.0; older owners cannot reopen 2.1. Any separately authorized deployment must preserve its pre-upgrade export, and recovery after new writes requires a compatible owner. No device writer changes.\n\n## Validation\n\nPassed on Node 24.21.0 / Python 3.14.4:\n\n- Build/typecheck, controller contracts in TypeScript/Python and package checks.\n- Lifecycle and agent-state TypeScript/Python corpora, provider/hook fixtures, migration/restart/freshness tests and isolated reproducible package checks.\n- MCP unit/protocol/package; Hub unit/package/MCP/setup checks.\n- Agent-status, Tidbyt TypeScript/Python, LIFX and local-controller suites.\n- Dashboard checks and full browser suite, including synthetic desktop/mobile title/project previews, explicit-label precedence, Unicode label bounds, search and untitled fallback.\n- Workflow checks/tests; all 18 specifications validate. Six deltas synchronized and archived.\n- Pinned Pixoo `28f4875b7a0f0e57ca6f25d9971e125e927a5503` and Nanoleaf `f3c13843f1e5431b01ddca344a91cd7484348f59` source checks: handoff, independent acknowledgments, late events and legacy/latest-state rollback. Simulator/disposable state only.\n\nTidbyt Python initially lacked Pillow; rerun passed using requirements-contracts.txt in an isolated test environment. Local receipts are under the coordinator's `.local/evidence/gh-424-session-titles/`.\n\n## Fixed comparison and reviews\n\nBase and merge-base: `490ad5ab3b8c47b2e82f1bbafd32b724e2b68f1f`.\nHead: `5d83200e2ead715a1120677fd06a8ffc959159d3` (two commits; clean worktree).\nDiff: `git diff 490ad5ab3b8c47b2e82f1bbafd32b724e2b68f1f 5d83200e2ead715a1120677fd06a8ffc959159d3`.\nThe initial Specification review had no findings. Standards found a P2 credential-pattern bypass after Unicode line separators; commit `5d83200` fixes it and adds shared regression canaries. Both independent reviewers passed this exact head with no remaining findings. Standards independently ran 168 Node tests plus both Python corpora; Specification independently ran 169 Node contract/state/provider/HTTP tests. The P2 is closed. Explicit approval of the current dashboard candidate is pending and required before merge.\n\n## Delivery\n\nAll six configured exact-head Depot jobs passed, with no annotations; both independent reviews passed. Main advanced to `0eb7474ce9d76bc0c928a17da0c5fd23288f9f7b` through a guide-only PR, and both reviewers confirmed no scope overlap or affected product-test requirement. UI approval, guarded merge, main CI and immutable package publication remain pending. #424 remains open because its installed Codex Desktop and Claude observations are not authorized or verified by source fixtures. Guide assessment sections remain coordinated with Goal 4; no guide refresh is part of this PR.\n",
    "state": "open",
